vkquake wm-info: non-fatal on a backend without native window handles

vkQuake 1.05.3 fetches SDL_GetWindowWMInfo into a global at window
creation and Sys_Errors on failure -- but the global is WRITE-ONLY on
every platform (even the Win32 full-screen-exclusive path fetches its
own local copy), so the error is the call's entire effect. Thylacine's
SDL backend has no native WM handle to report and returns unsupported;
hit live at the first W-4 local smoke, one line past the 0002 fix.
Downgrade to a Con_Printf.

--- a/Quake/gl_vidsdl.c	2026-08-31 16:02:15
+++ b/Quake/gl_vidsdl.c	2026-08-31 16:02:15
@@ -420,9 +420,13 @@
 		if (!draw_context)
 			Sys_Error ("Couldn't create window: %s", SDL_GetError());
 
+		/* Non-fatal: sys_wm_info is write-only on every platform (the
+		 * Win32 full-screen-exclusive path fetches its own local copy),
+		 * and a backend without native WM handles -- Thylacine's -- has
+		 * nothing to report. */
 		SDL_VERSION(&sys_wm_info.version);
 		if(!SDL_GetWindowWMInfo(draw_context,&sys_wm_info))
-			Sys_Error ("Couldn't get window wm info: %s", SDL_GetError());
+			Con_Printf ("SDL_GetWindowWMInfo not supported: %s\n", SDL_GetError());
 
 		previous_display = -1;
 	}
